# Initial Setup's ESC Calibration page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigESCCalibration.cs.
#
# The claim: the page shows the .resx's words - the heading, the Calibrate ESCs button and beside
# it the instructions that begin "Remove Props!" - and Activate sets up the ESC type and the five
# motor numbers from the vehicle (ConfigESCCalibration.cs:15-26). The page's one action, the
# button, sets ESC_CALIBRATION to 3 (:28-45); SITL has no ESCs, so this script never presses it,
# and proves that showing the page, and leaving it, sends nothing: the page's count of sets is 0
# and the vehicle's ESC_CALIBRATION is still 0 at the end. The press itself is covered by the unit
# tests in crates/mp-gui/src/config/esc_calibration.rs, against a scripted vehicle.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, whose motor
# parameters are the firmware's defaults: MOT_PWM_TYPE 0, MOT_PWM_MIN 1000, MOT_PWM_MAX 2000,
# MOT_SPIN_ARM 0.1, MOT_SPIN_MIN 0.15, MOT_SPIN_MAX 0.95. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-esc.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
settle 6
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.ESC_CALIBRATION 0

click tab-setup
expect config.esc.active false
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigESCCalibration
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigESCCalibration
expect config.esc.active true

# The page's words.
expect config.esc.heading ESC Calibration (AC3.3+)
expect config.esc.button Calibrate ESCs
expect config.esc.button.enabled true
expect config.esc.text ~ Remove Props!
expect config.esc.text ~ -Disconnect USB and battery
expect config.esc.text ~ -ESCs should beep as they are calibrated

# What Activate read.
expect config.esc.type 0
expect config.esc.type.text Normal
expect config.esc.type.enabled true
expect config.esc.mot_pwm_min 1000
expect config.esc.mot_pwm_max 2000
expect config.esc.mot_spin_arm 0.10
expect config.esc.mot_spin_min 0.15
expect config.esc.mot_spin_max 0.95
expect config.esc.mot_spin_max.enabled true

# Nothing sent: the button was not pressed.
settle 2
expect config.esc.sent 0
expect config.esc.calibration none
expect config.esc.write none
expect params.value.ESC_CALIBRATION 0

# Leaving the page sends nothing either.
click setup-page-ConfigFlightModes
expect setup.page ConfigFlightModes
expect config.esc.active false
settle 2
expect config.esc.sent 0
expect params.value.ESC_CALIBRATION 0
